{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_domsyncgl", "label": "DomSyncGL (API doc)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "lines 1-26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_ready", "label": "ready (async init Promise)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Properties > ready", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Awaiting is optional: before init completes render() is a no-op while createPlane()/update() are safe because update() never touches the GPU. It rejects only when neither WebGPU nor WebGL 2 is available."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_iswebgpubackend", "label": "isWebGPUBackend()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > isWebGPUBackend", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns false before ready resolves because the backend is only decided after async init - callers must await ready before branching on it."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_tick", "label": "tick(time?)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > tick", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A thin facade over update() then render(); time is accepted only for API symmetry with Lenis since elapsed time actually comes from an internal THREE.Clock."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_update_render", "label": "update(time?) / render(options?)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > update / render", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Splitting state update from draw lets render() save and restore whatever RenderTarget was bound before the call and write only to outputTarget, so multiple scenes can be drawn into external FBOs for transitions without corrupting them."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_createplane", "label": "createPlane(selector, options?)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > createPlane", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_createtextplane", "label": "createTextPlane(selector, options?)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > createTextPlane", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_create3dobject", "label": "create3DObject(selector, options)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > create3DObject", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_addeffect", "label": "addEffect / removeEffect / clearEffects", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > addEffect", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_setposteffect", "label": "setPostEffect(effectLike, options?)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > setPostEffect", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ownership defaults to domSyncGL (it disposes the previous postEffect on replace/clearEffects/destroy); { owned: false } hands dispose back to the caller. Mixing it with addEffect() destroys the internal EffectComposer, so it throws in DEV."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_effectsamples", "label": "effectSamples (MSAA)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Options", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MSAA on the scene RenderTarget prevents jagged edges once effects are enabled; clamped to the GPU limit or the WebGPU standard 4 when the limit cannot be read."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_stats_gui_injection", "label": "stats.js / lil-gui instance injection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Options tip", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "showStats / showGUI / statsParent / guiTitle were removed: creation, DOM insertion and disposal are the caller's responsibility so the library merely uses the instance handed to it, and dev tools can be dynamic-imported out of the production bundle."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_enableorbitcontrols", "label": "enableOrbitControls()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Methods > enableOrbitControls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Under scrollSync the container has pointer-events: none, so orbit controls re-enable pointer events on the canvas only."}, {"id": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_getters", "label": "DomSyncGL getters (scene/camera/renderer/mouse/scroll)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Getters", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_domsyncgl", "target": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_ready", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "Properties", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_iswebgpubackend", "target": "docs_api_dom_sync_gl_ready", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/api/dom-sync-gl.md", "source_location": "isWebGPUBackend", "weight": 1.0}, {"sou